-The upstream release was imported without generated build files. The local
-source changes represented by the initial import are also preserved as:
+The upstream release and the local legacy-i386 changes are separate commits.
+The two functional commits after `upstream-1.2.6` are:
 
-- `patches/musl-1.2.6-i386-tas-lock.patch`
-- `patches/musl-1.2.6-i386-static-profile.patch`
+- `i386: implement internal locks with test-and-set`
+- `i386: add static low-memory profile`
 
-Those patches are provenance records only. The source in this directory is
-the build input and the authoritative maintained version.
+This repository's commit history is the authoritative maintained source.
+The parent `linux-pc98` repository also keeps exact `git format-patch`
+exports under `toolchain/patchsets/musl/1.2.6/`. Those exports are the
+portable provenance and review record; there is intentionally no second
+patch copy in this repository.
 
